==Trivia ==
*Goblins are small, grotesque, monstrous creatures that appear in the folklore of multiple European cultures. First attested in stories from the Middle Ages, they are ascribed conflicting abilities, temperaments, and appearances depending on the story and country of origin, ranging from mischievous household spirits to malicious, bestial thieves. They often have magical abilities similar to a fairy or demon, such as the ability to shapeshift. Similar creatures include [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duende duendes], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kobold kobolds], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun leprechauns], and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul ghouls].
**In the German and Dutch language setting of the game, the Goblin Hut's name translates to "Kobold Hut". In the Spanish, Norwegian, Arabic, Finnish, and Vietnamese language setting of the game, the Goblin Hut's name translates to "Duende Hut", "Goblin Cabin", "Ghoul Hut", "Goblin Lodge", and "Leprechaun Tent" respectively.
**The Goblin Hut is 1 of 17 [[cards]] associated with [[Goblins]], with the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblin Gang]], [[Baby Goblins]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Goblin Demolisher]], [[Suspicious Bush]], [[Goblin Cage]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Goblin Curse]], [[Goblin Drill]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Party Rocket]], [[Party Hut]], [[Goblinstein]], and of course, Goblins.
***The Goblins, Spear Goblins, Goblin Cage and Goblin Hut are the only cards associated with Goblins that are unlocked in Goblin Stadium.
*The Goblin Hut is 1 of 7 [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Tesla]], [[Inferno Tower]], [[Elixir Collector]], and [[X-Bow]].
**The Goblin Hut resembles its respective counterpart from the Single Player Campaign, in Clash of Clans. However, in Clash of Clans, the Goblin Hut does not spawn Spear Goblins or any troop for that matter.
*While not available as a building in Squad Busters, the Goblin Hut reappears there as a decoration.
*The Goblin Hut is one of the first building [[cards]] to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the Cannon, [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], Inferno Tower, and [[Barbarian Hut]].
*The Goblin Hut is one of the first building cards to receive a card render, alongside the Mortar, Tesla, and Goblin Cage.
*The Goblin Hut is 1 of 23 cards that has had its Elixir cost changed, the others being [[Bomber]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Royal Recruits]], Cannon, Mortar, [[Musketeer]], [[Three Musketeers]], [[Heal]], Bomb Tower, Barbarian Hut, [[Furnace]], Elixir Collector, [[Skeleton Army]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Electro Giant]], [[Bowler]], Goblin Barrel, [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Rage]], [[Fisherman]], and the [[Monk]].
*Its [[Star Points|Star Level 3 Skin]] grants the Spear Goblins a red mohawk similar to the Level 6 Goblin in Clash of Clans.
*In the Clash Royale [https://youtu.be/QoG41jI12bY Goblin Hut commercial], it is revealed what apparently goes on inside the Goblin Hut: a Goblin dance party.
*The Goblin Hut can be seen on the [[Trophies|Trophy Road]] as a decoration.
* During [[Clan Wars]], a Goblin Hut appears at the bottom-left side of the river, giving the player statistics about Clan War mechanics when tapped on.
* The Goblin Hut is 1 of 2 buildings that has been featured with a [[Buff#Shield%20Boost|Shield Boost]] [[buff]], the other being Goblin Cage.
*The Goblin Hut is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 20 cards that is unavailable in [[Mirror]] mode, the others being [[Minions]], Cannon, Mortar, Tesla, Tombstone, Bomb Tower, Inferno Tower, Barbarian Hut, Furnace, Elixir Collector, [[Freeze]], [[Clone]], X-Bow, [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Little Prince]], and the Monk.
**It is unavailable in [[Global Spell|The Floor is Healing]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the Global Spell game mode, much like other building cards, as well as the [[Cannon Cart]].
*The Goblin Hut is the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].

